Business Requirements Document (BRD) & Functional Requirements Document (FRD)
Project Name: SutraSparsh UI/UX System Standardization: "Parchment Dawn" Theme & WCAG Contrast Remediation Document Version: 1.0.0 Target Platform: Mobile Web & Responsive Web App (React / PWA / Native Webview) Status: Approved for Implementation
1. Executive Summary & Problem Statement
1.1 Context & Background
SutraSparsh is an authentic sacred wisdom, philosophy, and Sanskrit corpus learning application (Bhagavad Gita, Patanjali Yoga Sutras, Upanishads). The application’s spiritual and reflective nature demands an organic, warm, and reverent atmosphere referred to as the "Parchment Dawn" visual design language.
1.2 Core Problem Identification
Recent audits and visual evidence (as seen across the active screens) demonstrate significant theme fragmentation and severe accessibility regressions:
1. Severe Contrast Deficit (Explore Tab / Screen 2):
   * The sub-hero card ("Don't just read the translation. Explore the word.") uses high-luminance golden/sand text (#F5DEB3 / #F3C068) directly on an off-white/parchment background (#FFFDF7 / #F8F3E6).
   * Body copy ("A translation tells you what a sentence means...") fades into the background with less than a 1.4:1 contrast ratio, causing total illegibility and severe WCAG 2.1 AA violations.
2. Inconsistent Component Theming:
   * Screen 1 (Today Screen): Displays a balanced, high-contrast, warm cream aesthetic with deep espresso typography (#2D1F17), warm amber badges, and crisp terracotta CTA buttons.
   * Screen 2 (Explore Screen): Inconsistently introduces an inverted, dark charcoal-brown gradient hero card juxtaposed against washed-out, illegible parchment elements below it, breaking continuous visual flow.
3. Absence of Unified Design Tokens:
   * Colors are currently hardcoded or weakly scoped, leading to accidental bleeding of light accents into light container surfaces.
2. Business Case & Objectives (BRD)
2.1 Strategic Business Goals
* Improve Readability & Engagement Time: Eliminate visual strain during prolonged contemplative reading and recitation sessions.
* WCAG 2.1 AA & AAA Compliance: Ensure all textual content meets a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for regular text and 3.0:1 for large text/interactive UI boundaries.
* Brand Cohesion & Emotional Resonance: Deliver an uninterrupted, sacred, tactile "Parchment & Incense" feeling that matches the meditative discipline of Patanjali and the Upanishads.
* Reduce Bounce & Abandonment: Prevent drop-offs caused by illegible content on discovery and search paths.
