	4. Functional Requirements Document (FRD)
4.1 Global Architectural Changes
FR-01: Global CSS Custom Properties & Semantic Token Engine
* All hardcoded hex values across .jsx, .tsx, or .css modules must be replaced with semantic CSS tokens or Tailwind utility classes mapped to the Parchment Dawn palette.
* Under no circumstances shall yellow (#F..., #FFD700, etc.) be assigned to the color CSS property on light canvas surfaces.
:root {
 /* Parchment Dawn Foundation */
 --color-canvas-bg: #FBF8EE;
 --color-surface-card: #FFFDF8;
 --color-surface-subtle: #F5EEDB;
 --color-border-subtle: #E8DCC2;
 --color-border-highlight: #DECB9F;

 /* Typography Hierarchy */
 --color-text-title: #261B12;
 --color-text-body: #4A3A2F;
 --color-text-muted: #6E5C4E;
 --color-text-sacred-accent: #A64E04;

 /* Interactive Elements */
 --color-action-primary: #E05A1B;
 --color-action-primary-hover: #C54C13;
 --color-action-primary-text: #FFFFFF;
 --color-action-secondary-bg: #FDF3DF;
 --color-action-secondary-text: #874606;
 --color-action-secondary-border: #E8CF9A;
}

4.2 Component-Specific Functional Requirements
FR-02: Discovery & Banner Cards (Remediating Image 2 Regression)
* Target Component: DiscoveryCard, LookCloserHero, SacredCorpusBanner.
* Requirements:
   1. If a card utilizes a light parchment background (#FFFDF8):
      * The category badge pill must use bg-[#FBEFD3] text-[#874606] border-[#E8CF9A].
      * The primary heading ("Don't just read the translation...") must be rendered in text-espresso-primary (#261B12) or high-contrast deep saffron (#A64E04), never pale gold.
      * The display cursive/emphasis ("Explore the word.") must use deep burnt saffron (#B85002), guaranteeing a minimum 5.2:1 contrast ratio against the card canvas.
      * The descriptive body copy must use text-espresso-secondary (#4A3A2F), replacing the invisible light-grey/beige font.
   2. If the card uses the deep charcoal/amber dusk gradient (as seen in the top hero of Image 2):
      * The background gradient must remain consistently dark: linear-gradient(135deg, #231C18 0%, #352B23 60%, #4D382A 100%).
      * Text inside this dark card must remain light-gold (#FBE29D for headings, #DAC5B0 for body) with contrast exceeding 7:1 against the dark background.
FR-03: Shloka & Sanskrit Card Rendering (Standardizing Image 1)
* Target Component: DailyShlokaCard, ScriptureReader.
* Requirements:
   1. Devanagari script (अभ्यासवैराग्याभ्यां तन्निरोधः ॥) must maintain crisp, deep contrast (#1E1610) with distinct font-weight (\ge 600) to guarantee legibility of vowel signs (matras) and conjunct characters.
   2. IAST Romanized transliteration must render in italicized deep warm taupe (#544134).
   3. Word-by-word interactive chips ("Tap any word above to Look Closer") must pair a burnt amber icon with #824300 text, ensuring accessibility compliance while retaining the sacred glowing aesthetic.
   4. Card elevation must feature a soft ambient shadow: box-shadow: 0 4px 20px -2px rgba(80, 50, 20, 0.06), 0 0 0 1px rgba(222, 203, 159, 0.4).
FR-04: Action Buttons & Navigation Elements
* Target Component: BottomNavbar, StreakCounter, AudioControls.
* Requirements:
   1. Primary Button: Warm Terracotta/Saffron gradient (linear-gradient(180deg, #E66020 0%, #D44E0E 100%)) with white text (#FFFFFF) and warm drop shadow.
   2. Secondary Button ("Look Closer"): #FFF7E6 background, #D8A856 border, and #783C00 text with sparkles icon.
   3. Bottom Navigation Bar: Ensure inactive tabs (Explore, Search, Community, Journey, More) have #69574A color with proper labels, transitioning to #C65507 when active with a warm glowing pill backdrop.
