6. Acceptance Criteria & QA Checklist
6.1 Contrast & Accessibility Validation
* [ ] AC-01: Automated Axe core / Google Lighthouse accessibility tests run across all routes without any contrast violations (minimum score: 98).
* [ ] AC-02: All Devanagari text renders with crisp edges and is readable in bright ambient light settings.
* [ ] AC-03: The subtitle and body copy under "Don't just read the translation. Explore the word." in the Explore tab is verified at \ge 4.5:1 contrast against the container card surface.
6.2 Theme Consistency
* [ ] AC-04: Background canvas color #FBF8EE is maintained uniformly when switching between Today, Explore, Community, and Journey tabs.
* [ ] AC-05: Pill buttons, audio speeds (0.85x), and streak badges adhere to the shared palette variables rather than isolated inline styles.
* [ ] AC-06: Dark mode or dark-tinted elements (e.g., top hero banner in Explore) are reserved strictly for high-impact contemplative showcases and maintain distinct high-contrast golden typography on dark grounds.
7. Migration & Rollout Plan
1. Phase 1: Token Centralization (Day 1-2)
   * Consolidate color palette into unified Tailwind/CSS variable definitions.
   * Deprecate rogue inline color styles.
2. Phase 2: Screen 2 Remediation (Day 2-3)
   * Refactor Explore tab cards to bind to the newly defined high-contrast Parchment Dawn tokens.
3. Phase 3: Visual Regression & Accessibility Audit (Day 4)
   * Perform automated contrast verification via Percy/Chromatic and Axe-core.
   * Validate readability on low-brightness OLED and LCD displays.
4. Phase 4: Production Release (Day 5)
   * Deploy updated layout across production builds.